179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (A per-frame model sees only a single snapshot. At onset or offset, that snapshot is ambiguous. For example, a slight mouth curl could be the beginning of happiness or disgust. Without knowing what came before, the model guesses. To make it more fair when comparing results, we will be averaging out the result for the per-frame CNN over the same number of frames \(i.e. 15\) that our CNN+Transformer model and CNN+LSTM model gets to see.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [86]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (A temporal model sees the trajectory. Knowing the face was neutral two seconds ago and is now slightly asymmetric lets the model make an informed prediction about what's developing.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [87]
>>
endobj
